1927 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.98 .82 .2]/P 1823 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[203.35298 461.3914 457.98799 461.3914 203.35298 450.0614 457.98799 450.0614]/Rect[200.68239 449.35328 460.65858 462.09953]/AP<</N 1928 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(VERDICT-DET-01: Did the detector reproduce? \(Figs. 7 and 8\) [Outcome open, impact high]\nWe do: Outcome open. Gate A \(experiment 0053, 2026-08-13\) called the detector Outcome A on two containments. One survives: at 39 dB-Hz the published Pd at Pfa 0.05 \(0.84 by hand, 0.86 by script\) lies between our per-map 0.58 and per-cell 1.00 \(RES-FIG7-39-01\). The other does not: the published 36 dB-Hz curve exists only at Pfa 0.63 to 0.90 and was set against our values at Pfa 0.05, so the 36 dB-Hz match and the 6 dB figure are withdrawn \(RES-FIG7-36-01\). At matched Pfa against Sensors Fig. 6, our per-tile detector looks about 4 to 5 dB stronger \(RES-SENSORS6-01, an eye reading\). So the detector matches the published ordering and one operating point inside a wide band, and may be stronger than published by a margin we cannot yet explain. That is neither Outcome A nor Outcome B.\nIf we got it wrong: Called A too early, we benchmark and deploy a detector that may be several dB stronger than the published one, and every comparison against Borhani-Darian on TEXBAT or OAKBAT overstates their method. Called B too early, we disown a reconstruction that may differ only in a convention.\nTo close: Close the rows it waits on, then restate. EVAL-CASE-01 \(batch D\) reads per-map Pd at the published Pfa. RES-SENSORS6-01 \(batch B\) sizes the gap at matched Pfa. CAF-STDDET-02 with SIG-CN0DEF-01 \(batch A\) tests whether the gap is a C/N0 convention. TRAIN-LABELS-01 \(reading first\) checks that the network learns the published task. A person confirms the figure readings \(confirmed_by\) before the outcome changes.)/T(VERDICT-DET-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

