1932 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.98 .82 .2]/P 1823 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[185.083 449.3914 489.99705 449.3914 185.083 438.0614 489.99705 438.0614]/Rect[182.4124 437.35328 492.66764 450.09953]/AP<</N 1933 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(VERDICT-COUNT-01: Did the counting stage reproduce? \(Figs. 6 and 9\) [Outcome open, impact high]\nWe do: Outcome open. Gate A called the counting stage Outcome B, method reproduced and performance not: 13 of 15 informative Fig. 9 points fail the pre-registered rule \(RES-FIG9-01\). The ledger withdraws the first half of that. Our GMM counter finds one peak in only 1 of 20 one-peak control maps and calls 99.75% of clean 45 dB-Hz maps spoofed, where connected components on the same maps calls 0.06% \(COUNT-POINTS-01, COUNT-EM-01\). A counter that fails its own control has not reproduced the method, so the stage has not reached Outcome B, and the 13 failures may be ours.\nIf we got it wrong: If the failure is our fit, M1 and M1.1 both tell readers that a published method fails where only our implementation of it does. That is the claim a reviewer, or the authors, can most easily refute.\nTo close: First re-gate the counter: COUNT-POINTS-01 and COUNT-EM-01 on the one-peak and two-peak controls, then COUNT-FIG6-01 against the published clusters. Only a counter that passes the controls reruns Fig. 9 \(RES-FIG9-01, under both bin readings of CAF-DOPSTEP-02\), at stride 1 and with more than one model seed. Hamza signs off the 0.10 equivalence margin the scoring uses; it was pre-registered in 0053 and has never been signed off.)/T(VERDICT-COUNT-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

