1936 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.95 .55 .15]/P 55 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[350.69447 195.14063 477.64356 195.14063 350.69447 180.60724 477.64356 180.60724]/Rect[347.2688 179.6989 481.0692 196.04897]/AP<</N 1937 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(SIG-MODEL-01: How many satellites are in one simulated snapshot [Deviates, impact low]\nWe do: Each snapshot holds one satellite, plus a spoofed copy of it when spoofed, plus noise.\nIf we got it wrong: Small. GPS codes are designed so another satellite leaks in at roughly 24 dB below the peak, so the noise floor rises only slightly. This cannot explain the strength gap. It matters more on real recordings than on synthetic ones.\nTo close: Closed: one satellite per snapshot is accepted \(the group simulates one satellite for per-satellite processing, Li 2020\); no ablation.)/T(SIG-MODEL-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

