1948 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 111 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[153.39345 676.0894 233.37029 676.0894 153.39345 661.556 233.37029 661.556]/Rect[149.96779 660.6477 236.79595 676.99777]/AP<</N 1949 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A4)/Contents(SIG-DELAYFRAC-01: Code delay only on whole samples [Paper silent, our choice, impact medium]\nWe do: Delays are whole samples, so the true peak always lands exactly on a cell of the delay grid.\nIf we got it wrong: Our signal looks slightly stronger than theirs at the same C/N0. My estimate at 4 MHz: up to about 1.2 dB at worst, about 0.6 dB on average. It pushes in the direction of the strength gap, so it is a real contributor, but not the whole gap.\nTo close: Ablation: shift the code by a random fraction of a sample and rerun the faithful arm.)/T(SIG-DELAYFRAC-01)/BM/Multiply>>
