1960 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.6378 458.7324 247.28199 458.7324 117.6378 444.199 247.28199 444.199]/Rect[114.212139 443.29069 250.70764 459.64073]/AP<</N 1961 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(SIG-SIMULATOR-01: Which signal simulator, and what it models [Paper silent, our choice, impact high]\nWe do: Ideal baseband: an unfiltered, unquantized, perfect copy of the code plus noise.\nIf we got it wrong: Possibly a large part of the strength gap. Rough textbook figures: front-end filtering loses about 0.5 to 1 dB, 2-bit quantization about 0.5 dB, 1-bit about 2 dB. Together with the fractional-delay loss that is a few dB, all in the direction of the gap.\nTo close: Reading first: search the thesis and the Sensors paper for the simulator's name and front-end settings. Then an ablation with a front-end filter and quantization.)/T(SIG-SIMULATOR-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

