1976 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.35 .78 .45]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[353.0418 246.48358 477.61946 246.48358 353.0418 231.9502 477.61946 231.9502]/Rect[349.61616 231.04186 481.0451 247.39192]/AP<</N 1977 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A8)/Contents(TRAIN-SIZE-01: How much training data [Verified, impact medium]\nWe do: 3000 training tiles \(the p11 reading\).\nIf we got it wrong: Measured in part: doubling to 6000 tiles raises Pd at 36 dB-Hz from 0.931 to 0.955. The 10^4 reading would likely raise it further, which moves us away from their curve, not toward it. The "hundreds" reading would lower it, toward their curve. So the size could explain part of the gap only if the thesis's smallest reading is the true one.\nTo close: Nothing left to read: 3000 pairs is the faithful size and ours matches. The 10^4 arm is dropped; a few-hundred arm stays optional.)/T(TRAIN-SIZE-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

