1984 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[285.412 232.3324 455.24296 232.3324 285.412 217.79901 455.24296 217.79901]/Rect[281.98634 216.89067 458.6686 233.24074]/AP<</N 1985 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A12)/Contents(REAL-CN0-01: Real satellites' C/N0 against the training range of 36 to 45 dB-Hz [Not done, impact medium]\nWe do: Not measured per satellite for any faithful run. A recording holds satellites at many strengths, from low elevation to near zenith, and the spoofed signal has a C/N0 of its own.\nIf we got it wrong: Mixing satellites inside and outside the training range blurs the real-data numbers, and an offset in their C/N0 convention would make the synthetic-to-real comparison look better or worse than it is.\nTo close: Test: estimate C/N0 for every tracked satellite on the clean segments, then report real-data results by C/N0 band and flag satellites outside 36 to 45 dB-Hz.)/T(REAL-CN0-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

