<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.95 .55 .15]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[147.17548 159.59918 166.86052 159.59918 147.17548 149.7959 166.86052 149.7959 166.5929 161.58362 284.2115 161.58362 166.5929 147.05023 284.2115 147.05023]/Rect[144.86475 146.14189 287.63716 162.49196]/AP<</N 2001 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A20)/Contents(SIG-DOPRANGE-01: Range of random Doppler shifts [Deviates, impact low]\nWe do: Training draws -3500 to 3500 Hz and scoring -3000 to 3000 Hz. The paper uses -4000 to 4000 Hz.\nIf we got it wrong: Small. Tiles look the same wherever the peak sits in Doppler, except near the edges. On our axis, +4000 Hz is bin 45, one past the last bin a centred tile can use \(44\), so the paper's top-edge peaks would sit slightly off-centre. A few percent of samples at most.\nTo close: Fix: use the stated range in the next faithful run.)/T(SIG-DOPRANGE-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

