2004 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.95 .55 .15]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.64189 147.43238 337.2304 147.43238 117.64189 132.89899 337.2304 132.89899]/Rect[114.216228 131.99065 340.65608 148.34072]/AP<</N 2005 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A22)/Contents(REAL-DOPWIPE-01: Removing the Doppler before the CAF: our real-data path does it, the paper does not [Deviates, impact medium]\nWe do: real_caf first runs a separate acquisition \(acquire: 250 Hz steps over plus or minus 6 kHz, using 5 ms\), removes that coarse Doppler, and only then forms the 50 x 200 Hz CAF, so the peak always sits near the middle of the grid. real_caf_snapshots estimates the Doppler once and reuses it for all six snapshots.\nIf we got it wrong: Real-data Pd and Pfa would describe a two-stage receiver, classic acquisition followed by the network, rather than the published method. On clean data it also removes the cases where a peak half-leaves the grid, so false-alarm rates may look better than the faithful method would give.\nTo close: Test: run the faithful model on the same real segments twice, with the pre-wipe and on the paper's fixed grid \(the CAF-DOPAXIS-01 axis\). Report how many satellite-epochs fall outside the grid's usable interior without the wipe, and how Pd and Pfa move.)/T(REAL-DOPWIPE-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

