2008 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.35 .78 .45]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[407.98448 133.28119 477.61256 133.28119 407.98448 118.7478 477.61256 118.7478]/Rect[404.5588 117.83946 481.0382 134.18953]/AP<</N 2009 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A24)/Contents(CAF-FEATURE-01: What the network sees: CAF magnitude or CAF power? [Verified, impact medium]\nWe do: We feed the power, |CAF|^2. Our docs \(sim.py, and the glossary's |CAF|^2 entry\) justify this with eqs. \(5\) and \(8\), which describe the classic detector, not the network input. Fig. 2 is better support.\nIf we got it wrong: Our numbers shift by about 3 points \(Pd 0.931 with power against 0.962 with magnitude, at 36 dB-Hz and Pfa 0.05, five seeds, 0053\). Magnitude scores higher, which moves us further from their curve, not closer. So this cannot explain the strength gap, but it changes every number we report.\nTo close: A person checks Fig. 2's axis label on p8. If it reads as power, mark verified: the figure shows what the network is fed. Thesis eqs. 2.21 and 3.4 and Sensors eq. 13 are a second route if the figure is judged too indirect.)/T(CAF-FEATURE-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

