2012 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1000 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[190.15683 76.68237 313.49958 76.68237 190.15683 62.148988 313.49958 62.148988]/Rect[186.73117 61.24065 316.92524 77.59071]/AP<</N 2013 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A26)/Contents(CAF-DOPSTEP-01: Doppler bin width [Verified, impact medium]\nWe do: 200 Hz bins, as the main text says.\nIf we got it wrong: If their grid were really 500 Hz, their tiles would show a much narrower peak, and they would lose up to about 0.9 dB whenever the true Doppler falls between bins. That pushes their curves down a little. Medium impact, and checkable.\nTo close: Reading: the thesis and the Sensors paper may state the grid.\n\nCAF-DOPAXIS-01: Where the Doppler axis is centred [Paper silent, our choice, impact low]\nWe do: -5000 to +4800 Hz: 25 bins below zero, 24 above.\nIf we got it wrong: Negligible on its own. It only interacts with SIG-DOPRANGE-01: at +4000 Hz the peak sits one bin past where a centred tile can reach.\nTo close: Optional fix: a symmetric axis. Low priority.)/T(CAF-DOPSTEP-01 + CAF-DOPAXIS-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

