2052 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.35 .78 .45]/P 1066 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[335.5879 407.2406 477.60557 407.2406 335.5879 392.7072 477.60557 392.7072]/Rect[332.16224 391.7989 481.03123 408.14894]/AP<</N 2053 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A12)/Contents(NET-DROPOUT-01: Where dropout sits: after the two hidden layers only, or also at the output [Verified, impact low]\nWe do: Dropout 0.5 after FC1 and FC2 \(each after its ReLU\). The output layer is linear with no dropout. No dropout in the convolution layers.\nIf we got it wrong: If the literal text were right, a ReLU before the softmax would set both outputs to zero on many noise tiles, giving exactly 0.5 and 0.5, a ratio of 1. Many noise cells would then tie at the threshold gamma = 1, which reshapes the low-Pfa end of the ROC and what the counting stage sees. The figure argues against it, so our reading is the likely one.\nTo close: A person checks the labels under FC1, FC2 and FC_n\(2\) in journal Fig. 3 \(p9\).)/T(NET-DROPOUT-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

