<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1066 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[309.96324 147.16681 477.67063 147.16681 309.96324 132.63343 477.67063 132.63343]/Rect[306.53758 131.72509 481.09629 148.07515]/AP<</N 2061 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A16)/Contents(FUSE-PHASE-01: Carrier phase from one snapshot to the next [Paper silent, our choice, impact medium]\nWe do: Two policies in two scripts. Fig. 7/8 scoring \(run.py, run_fullscan.py\) draws both phases at random in every snapshot. Fig. 9 \(run_phase2.py, phase_policy: coherent\) draws one phase per trial for each signal and advances it by 2 pi fd k T in snapshot k, as a continuous carrier would.\nIf we got it wrong: For Fig. 7/8, nothing: our scored peaks sit 60 to 320 samples apart, where the cross-term stays below the code sidelobes \(gate-a-phase-fidelity.md\). For Fig. 9 at 0 Hz and 0 us the policy alone moves our L == 2 rate from 0.00 \(phase difference held at pi\) through 0.03 \(held at 0\) and 0.06 \(coherent\) to 0.30 \(drawn again per snapshot\), against a published 0.082. Coherent passes that point; drawing again fails it.\nTo close: Nothing in the sources settles it. Keep coherent as primary, since it is what consecutive milliseconds of one carrier do, and report Fig. 9's 0 and 1 us points with the phase bracket beside them.)/T(FUSE-PHASE-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

