<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1066 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.639308 104.715579 257.02375 104.715579 117.639308 90.18219 257.02375 90.18219]/Rect[114.21364 89.27385 260.4494 105.62392]/AP<</N 2069 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A20)/Contents(FUSE-SNAPSHOTS-01: How the six snapshots differ from each other [Paper silent, our choice, impact low]\nWe do: Six separate 1 ms simulations with the same delay, Doppler and spoofer geometry, and fresh noise each time. No delay drift, no data bits. Carrier phase is FUSE-PHASE-01.\nIf we got it wrong: Small. Over 6 ms a real signal's code drifts by about 0.02 chips at 4 kHz Doppler, far below one sample, so holding the delay fixed is physically right. A bit flip inside a snapshot would weaken that one snapshot's peak; with one flip per 20 ms at most, at most one of the six is hit \(SIG-NAVBITS-01\).\nTo close: Reading: a person agrees that "a distinct sub-image for each integration period" means consecutive periods of one signal; then mark verified.)/T(FUSE-SNAPSHOTS-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

