<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.62 .1 .35]/P 1701 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[146.5658 496.5675 301.94749 496.5675 146.5658 487.5035 301.94749 487.5035]/Rect[144.42932 486.937 304.08396 497.134]/AP<</N 2077 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(RES-FIG9-01: Fig. 9 \(finding both signals against their delay separation\): the counting stage does not reproduce [Tested, does not match, impact high]\nWe do: Phase 2 at 42 dB-Hz \(assumed\), stride-6 scan, one model seed, 300 maps per quantitative point, GMM+BIC, with "exactly two signals counted" as the event. Scored by a pre-registered rule: a per-point tolerance capped at 0.10, and an equivalence test on the mean difference.\nIf we got it wrong: The failure is large, not marginal. Misses run both ways, from +0.531 \(500 Hz apart, 1 microsecond: ours 0.73 against 0.199\) to -0.584 \(500 Hz, 3 microseconds: ours 0.38 against 0.964\). Our curves are not monotone in delay where theirs are. The two passing points are \(0 Hz, 0 microseconds\) 0.0633 against 0.082 and \(0 Hz, 3 microseconds\) 0.3167 against 0.359. Three choices the sources leave open could move every point: the C/N0, the bin reading, and stride 6 instead of 1.\nTo close: Test: rerun the sweep with a saved faithful model under the 200 Hz bin reading \(CAF-DOPSTEP-02\), at stride 1, and at 39 and 45 dB-Hz as well as 42, since Fig. 9's C/N0 is unstated.)/T(RES-FIG9-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

