<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1701 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.6378 385.38117 404.13978 385.38117 117.6378 370.84779 404.13978 370.84779]/Rect[114.212139 369.93946 407.56544 386.2895]/AP<</N 2085 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A6)/Contents(RES-OUTPERF-01: The claim that the network beats the standard detector [Not done, impact medium]\nWe do: Not tested. We have no classic detector \(CAF-STDDET-01\) and no theory curves \(CAF-STDDET-02\).\nIf we got it wrong: By my reading of Fig. 7 the claim holds only at 39 dB-Hz, in a narrow Pfa window: dashed 0.864 against solid 0.758 at Pfa 0.05. At 36 dB-Hz the dashed curve is far below the solid one, and at 42 and 45 both sit near 1. If one curve counts per map and the other per cell, the figure cannot support the claim either way.\nTo close: Experiment: build the classic detector on our maps \(CAF-STDDET-01\) and score it under the same false-alarm unit as our network, per cell and per map, against the faithful arm.)/T(RES-OUTPERF-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

