<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1701 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.6378 286.33119 342.18327 286.33119 117.6378 271.7978 342.18327 271.7978]/Rect[114.212139 270.88948 345.60893 287.2395]/AP<</N 2093 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A10)/Contents(REAL-TRAIN-01: What the network is trained on before it sees real data [Not done, impact high]\nWe do: Not done. The faithful reading is to train only on simulated tiles, as the faithful arm does, and apply the frozen model to the real recordings. M1's real-data runs did something else: 0011 and 0014 trained the peak detector on OAKBAT's clean recording, and M1's synthetic-to-OAKBAT transfer used the M1 pipeline, not the faithful arm.\nIf we got it wrong: Training on the target recordings would turn a test of the published method into a test of our own variant, and its numbers would sit in the wrong row of the benchmark.\nTo close: Test: run the frozen faithful model on OAKBAT and TEXBAT under REAL-THRESH-01 and REAL-EVENT-01. A real-trained arm, if we want one, is a separate variant with its own label.)/T(REAL-TRAIN-01)/BM/Multiply>>
