<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1701 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.6378 272.17994 313.63578 272.17994 117.6378 257.64656 313.63578 257.64656]/Rect[114.212139 256.73823 317.06144 273.08827]/AP<</N 2097 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A12)/Contents(REAL-SCENARIOS-01: Which scenarios, and how their spoofer power and separation compare with what the paper tested [Not done, impact medium]\nWe do: Not chosen for faithful runs. The datasets fix these values, from strong overpowered pushes to nearly matched power \(OAKBAT os2 at +10 dB, os4 at +0.4 dB\); the dataset-realism audit lists each scenario's power and timeline. Our synthetic spoofer in 0053 is 1 dB weaker than the real signal and 15 to 80 chips away from it, while OAKBAT's time pushes sit about 2 chips from the real peak \(0011\).\nIf we got it wrong: Choosing only easy scenarios flatters the published method; choosing only matched-power ones tests it outside anything it claims.\nTo close: Decide before any run: pre-register the scenario list for each dataset, with each scenario's measured power advantage and code separation over time, and report the results per scenario, in order of difficulty.)/T(REAL-SCENARIOS-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

