<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.35 .78 .45]/P 1537 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[341.1757 548.8906 474.05393 548.8906 341.1757 534.35726 474.05393 534.35726 117.6378 534.7406 141.98493 534.7406 117.6378 520.2072 141.98493 520.2072]/Rect[114.212139 519.2989 477.47959 549.79898]/AP<</N 2101 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(FUSE-K-01: Six snapshots are fused, and only at test time [Verified, impact low]\nWe do: K = 6 everywhere. The network trains on single-snapshot tiles; the six outputs are fused only when scoring.\nIf we got it wrong: Low. Sensors p13 is explicit: "While the training of the model was conducted using CAF images produced by 1 ms coherent integration times, the overall method was tested with and without noncoherent integration schemes". The journal's "In training" is most likely a slip for testing. My reading, not yet confirmed by a person.\nTo close: Reading: a person confirms that the journal's "In training" means testing, from Sensors p13.)/T(FUSE-K-01)/BM/Multiply>>
