2116 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.98 .82 .2]/P 1537 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[146.5658 100.252017 317.7553 100.252017 146.5658 91.18799 317.7553 91.18799]/Rect[144.42932 90.62149 319.89179 100.81851]/AP<</N 2117 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A8)/Contents(RES-FIG7-39-01: Fig. 7 at 39 dB-Hz: the one published detection point Gate A compares against [Implemented, unverified, impact high]\nWe do: Pd at Pfa 0.05 under three readings: per cell 0.9997 \(arm F, five seeds, sd 0.0003\); per 2000-cell map 0.969 \(three seeds\); per stride-6 full map 0.583 \(one seed, 60 maps\). Gate A calls the published value contained because it falls between 0.583 and 0.9997.\nIf we got it wrong: Containment is weak evidence. The band is 0.42 wide, and its lower end moves with how many cells a map has \(0.969 at 2000 cells, 0.583 at about 25,000\). The full-map value rests on 60 maps, so its Pfa 0.05 threshold is set by three maps. Separately, 0053's digitizer calibration is off by one tick label on the Pd axis, so its auto cross-check values and its recorded onset \(Pfa 0.0109\) are wrong. The hand-read targets were read by eye and agree with a corrected reading to within 0.026.\nTo close: Read by script in two passes \(check:fig7_39_two_pass\): Pd 0.92 at Pfa 0.10, 0.86 to 0.87 at Pfa 0.05. Remaining: fix targets_fig7.csv, calibration_fig7.json and targets_fig7_autocrosscheck.csv to these values. The per-map value at the paper's map size comes from the EVAL-CASE-01 scan.)/T(RES-FIG7-39-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

