2120 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.98 .82 .2]/P 720 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[146.5658 561.00747 266.78013 561.00747 146.5658 551.9435 266.78013 551.9435]/Rect[144.42932 551.37698 268.9166 561.574]/AP<</N 2121 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(TILE-FIG2-01: Fig. 2's axes do not fit the stated 4 MHz, 200 Hz grid [Implemented, unverified, impact medium]\nWe do: 4 MHz and 200 Hz bins, as the text states.\nIf we got it wrong: At 2 MHz each delay cell is half a chip wide, so whole-sample delay loss roughly doubles \(up to about 2.5 dB, about 1.2 dB on average\), and 500 Hz bins add up to 0.9 dB more. Their detector would then be weaker than ours at the same C/N0, the direction of the strength gap, and Fig. 9's "500 Hz" would be correct rather than a slip.\nTo close: Reading: thesis Fig. 3.11 \(the same figure\) and the thesis Ch.3 setup text. If the figures keep pointing at 2 MHz, an ablation: rerun the faithful arm on a 2 MHz, 500 Hz grid.)/T(TILE-FIG2-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

