2124 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 720 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[228.88674 348.82997 359.98924 348.82997 228.88674 334.29658 359.98924 334.29658]/Rect[225.46108 333.38825 363.4149 349.73829]/AP<</N 2125 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(REAL-PRNAGG-01: From one satellite's verdict to the receiver's verdict [Paper silent, our choice, impact medium]\nWe do: Nothing faithful yet. M1 pooled per-satellite scores across the tracked satellites \(constellation aggregation\), which helped position pushes most. That pooling is ours, not the paper's.\nIf we got it wrong: An aggregation rule tuned on the target data would be a hidden calibration step. A rule that is too strict or too loose moves the real-data Pd and Pfa by more than any change to the detector.\nTo close: Test: report per satellite first, which is the faithful result, then one pre-declared receiver rule \(spoofed if any satellite is called spoofed, and the stricter at-least-two variant\), both at gamma = 1. Count satellites per decision for the cost model.)/T(REAL-PRNAGG-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

