2128 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 720 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.63869 205.25733 309.70399 205.25733 117.63869 190.72394 309.70399 190.72394]/Rect[114.21302 189.8156 313.12965 206.16567]/AP<</N 2129 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A4)/Contents(FUSE-CLIP-01: What happens when the network is almost certain \(ratios near 0 or infinity\) [Paper silent, our choice, impact medium]\nWe do: We never form probabilities. We fuse logit differences, which equal log\(p1/p0\) exactly and cannot saturate. Nothing is clipped.\nIf we got it wrong: If their per-snapshot ratio saturates and ours does not, our fused scores separate peaks from noise better than theirs at the top of the range. Our detector would then look stronger than theirs, the direction of the strength gap. How often the real network reaches such a ceiling is not measured.\nTo close: Ablation on a saved faithful model, no retraining: rescore Fig. 7/8 with each snapshot's ratio formed in single precision as p1 / \(1 - p1\) and multiplied in single precision, and compare with our log-domain scores. The same run gives the histograms for FUSE-SCALE-01.)/T(FUSE-CLIP-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

