2132 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.98 .82 .2]/P 904 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[144.2154 577.03707 397.65025 577.03707 144.2154 562.50369 397.65025 562.50369]/Rect[140.78974 561.59536 401.0759 577.9454]/AP<</N 2133 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(NET-FAMILY-01: Which network produced the journal's results [Implemented, unverified, impact medium]\nWe do: Net A, our build of the Sensors 7-conv + 3-FC sub-image classifier, is the per-tile network in every Gate A arm. We never use the thesis Ch. 3.1 networks.\nIf we got it wrong: The full-CAF networks of thesis Ch. 3.1 are ruled out with good confidence: the journal works on 11 x 36 sub-images \(p9, p10, p11\) and p4 drops the full-CAF approach by name. What stays uncertain is the depth and widths of the sub-image network, if they changed it when moving from acquisition to spoofing. That would matter less than it sounds: on a different task \(0007, two-peak tiles\), a network with 60x fewer parameters scored within about 2 points of Net A at 36 dB-Hz \(0.932 nunes_tiny against 0.909 Net A, five seeds\).\nTo close: A person reads journal p9 and Sensors p13 side by side and confirms the deferral. Only the authors can confirm that the count carried over, and they have not answered outreach, so the practical close is to accept the deferral and write in the paper that the layer count comes from [47].)/T(NET-FAMILY-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

