<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1213 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[242.07727 545.73947 429.43757 545.73947 242.07727 531.20608 429.43757 531.20608]/Rect[238.65161 530.2977 432.86323 546.64779]/AP<</N 2137 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(REAL-THRESH-01: The threshold on real data: gamma = 1, fixed before any data is seen [Not done, impact high]\nWe do: Not done. The faithful choice is gamma = 1 on real data, set before seeing it. It is the one operating point that is frozen from the source by construction, which is what Hamza's threshold discipline \(technical correction 5\) asks for. A threshold picked on clean real data to reach 1% FAR is target-calibrated.\nIf we got it wrong: Reporting only a target-calibrated ROC point would overstate how the published method deploys. Reporting only gamma = 1 hides how much a calibrated receiver could recover.\nTo close: Test: report Pd and Pfa at gamma = 1 first, labelled source-frozen, then the ROC and Pd at 1% FAR with the threshold set on held-out clean segments, labelled target-calibrated.)/T(REAL-THRESH-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

