<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.95 .55 .15]/P 1213 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[177.35164 503.2894 288.03089 503.2894 177.35164 488.756 288.03089 488.756]/Rect[173.92598 487.8477 291.45655 504.19773]/AP<</N 2145 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A4)/Contents(EVAL-THRESH-01: The decision threshold: gamma = 1 by design, but no published point shows it [Deviates, impact medium]\nWe do: Phase 1 reports Pd at a matched Pfa of 0.05, 0.10 and 0.20, setting the threshold from the noise scores. It never reports gamma = 1. Phase 2 counts at gamma = 1.\nIf we got it wrong: Medium. Matched Pfa is a fair way to compare ROC curves, so no Gate A number is wrong because of it. But the paper's own operating point is never compared, and the plots stop at 4 x 10^-4, where the Pfa floors are already reached \(0.0375 at 39 dB-Hz, 0.0106 at 42\).\nTo close: Test: in the next faithful-arm run, also report Pd and Pfa at gamma = 1 \(fused log-ratio 0\) and save the fused scores, so our Pfa\(gamma\) can be laid over journal Fig. 8 and Sensors Fig. 7.)/T(EVAL-THRESH-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

