<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.95 .55 .15]/P 1481 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[133.5953 631.9145 326.0555 631.9145 133.5953 617.3811 326.0555 617.3811]/Rect[130.16965 616.4728 329.48118 632.8228]/AP<</N 2149 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(COUNT-BICN-01: BIC's n: every cell above threshold, or a subsample of 2000 [Deviates, impact low]\nWe do: Every cell above threshold, unless more than 2000 pass; then a seeded random 2000 of them, so n = 2000.\nIf we got it wrong: Probably nothing at gamma = 1, where a peak's blob is tens of cells. The cap can only bind at the very low thresholds of the false-alarm fit \(down to 10^-8\), where thousands of cells may pass. That is an inference: the run discards the number of passing cells \(run_phase2.py:205\), so we cannot say how often the cap bound.\nTo close: Test: log the number of passing cells per map in the next counting run and report how often it exceeds 2000.)/T(COUNT-BICN-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

