2152 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.95 .55 .15]/P 1481 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[265.9651 617.7657 423.37165 617.7657 265.9651 603.2323 423.37165 603.2323]/Rect[262.53944 602.324 426.7973 618.674]/AP<</N 2153 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(COUNT-BICPARAMS-01: BIC's parameter count: the printed m = 6K cannot be meant literally [Deviates, impact low]\nWe do: scikit-learn's own count for a 2-D mixture with full covariances: 6L - 1 \(per component 2 mean values, 3 covariance values and 1 weight, minus 1 because the weights sum to 1\).\nIf we got it wrong: Low. 6L and 6L - 1 differ by a constant, which never changes which L wins. The paper itself supports the 6L reading: 6 is exactly the count per component of a 2-D Gaussian with full covariance plus a mixing weight. That also says they fitted weights, although eq. \(12\) is printed without them \(as printed it is not a probability density: it integrates to L\). The literal reading would make every Fig. 9 map count the maximum L, at least 3 since Fig. 6 needs 3, and Fig. 9's Pd near 1 rules that out.\nTo close: Reading: a person agrees that m = 6K is a typo for 6L. The row then stays a deviation from the printed text only.)/T(COUNT-BICPARAMS-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

