2156 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1481 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[413.9604 447.96449 477.64073 447.96449 413.9604 433.4311 477.64073 433.4311]/Rect[410.53474 432.52278 481.06639 448.8728]/AP<</N 2157 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A4)/Contents(COUNT-THRESH-01: Which cells reach the GMM: the map and its threshold [Paper silent, our choice, impact high]\nWe do: The fused K = 6 log-ratio map on the stride-6 grid, thresholded at gamma = 1 \(fused > 0\) for Fig. 9 and the counting control. The false-alarm fit also sweeps gamma from 10^-8 to 10^4.\nIf we got it wrong: Likely large. Fig. 6c \(p14, 42 dB-Hz\) shows about 7 points per signal, in one delay column. Ours, at gamma = 1, splits single peaks: L = 1 in only 1 of 20 one-peak control maps at 45 dB-Hz, where connected components gets 20 of 20 \(results_phase2.json, g3_control\). A stricter threshold would shrink our blobs toward theirs.\nTo close: Experiment: rerun the 45 dB-Hz counting control \(20 one-peak and 20 two-peak maps\) and count each map at gamma = 1, 10^2, 10^4 and 10^6; then rerun the Fig. 9 sweep at the threshold that counts the control right.)/T(COUNT-THRESH-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

