2160 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1481 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[227.3964 89.972049 379.71406 89.972049 227.3964 80.90802 379.71406 80.90802]/Rect[225.25992 80.34152 381.85054 90.53854]/AP<</N 2161 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A6)/Contents(COUNT-FIG6-01: We never compared our thresholded clusters with Fig. 6 [Not done, impact high]\nWe do: Never compared. Our only cluster-level evidence is the counting control: one or two well-separated peaks at 45 dB-Hz.\nIf we got it wrong: Our counter splits single peaks. At 45 dB-Hz it finds L = 1 in 1 of 20 one-peak maps \(L = 2 in 8, 3 in 10, 4 in 1\) and flags 99.75% of 1,600 clean maps as spoofed; connected components finds 1 in 20 of 20 and flags 0.06%. Their Fig. 6c shows three clean clusters. Unless our blobs look like theirs, Gate A's counting verdict compares two different inputs.\nTo close: Test: build our fused map for Fig. 6's setup \(42 dB-Hz, one signal and two spoofers\), threshold it at gamma = 1, plot it like Fig. 6c, and report points per cluster and delay width. Do the same for one clean 45 dB-Hz control map.)/T(COUNT-FIG6-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

