<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1332 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[117.6378 452.49058 281.87498 452.49058 117.6378 437.95719 281.87498 437.95719]/Rect[114.212139 437.04887 285.30064 453.3989]/AP<</N 2169 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(REAL-COUNTER-01: M1's OAKBAT counting results used the counter that fails its control [Not done, impact high]\nWe do: The same function, count_signals_gmm, produced M1's counting results on real data: 0011 \(the OAKBAT ladder's peak-count decision\) and 0014 \(counting on OAKBAT, the source of the "counting discredited" line\). On synthetic maps it finds one peak in only 1 of 20 one-peak controls \(COUNT-POINTS-01, COUNT-EM-01\). Those M1 results have not been rechecked.\nIf we got it wrong: M1 and M1.1 would both tell readers that a published method fails where only our implementation of it fails.\nTo close: Test: once the counter passes its synthetic controls \(the first step of VERDICT-COUNT-01\), rerun 0014's hardened counting on OAKBAT with the fixed counter and compare with the committed numbers. 0014 also scored connected components, so part of its comparison may survive as it is.)/T(REAL-COUNTER-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

