<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1332 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[221.81182 438.33937 399.37528 438.33937 221.81182 423.80598 399.37528 423.80598]/Rect[218.38616 422.89765 402.80094 439.24769]/AP<</N 2173 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A4)/Contents(COUNT-POINTS-01: Does the GMM see cell positions only, or positions weighted by probability? [Paper silent, our choice, impact high]\nWe do: Positions only. Every cell above threshold is one point \(Doppler in Hz, delay in samples\) with equal weight. Both coordinates are standardized before fitting.\nIf we got it wrong: A candidate main cause of the counting failure. Our counter calls 99.75% of 1,600 clean 45 dB-Hz maps spoofed at gamma = 1, where connected components on the same maps \(any blob of one cell or more\) calls 0.06% \(results_phase2.json, fit, cn0_45\).\nTo close: Experiment: add a weighted variant \(each cell weighted by its fused ratio, or by its log-ratio\) and rerun the 45 dB-Hz counting control; rerun Fig. 9 if it counts the control right.)/T(COUNT-POINTS-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

