2184 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 1332 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[232.30664 104.71802 448.99049 104.71802 232.30664 90.18463 448.99049 90.18463]/Rect[228.88098 89.27629 452.41615 105.62636]/AP<</N 2185 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A10)/Contents(COUNT-EM-01: EM settings for the GMM fit \(start, restarts, regularization\) [Paper silent, our choice, impact high]\nWe do: scikit-learn GaussianMixture with full covariances and reg_covar = 1e-3 \(added to each covariance diagonal, in standardized units\), plus its defaults: one k-means start \(n_init = 1\), at most 100 iterations, tolerance 1e-3. random_state is the model seed \(0\) for every map. None of this is written in our docs or in the Gate A write-up; it lives only in the code.\nIf we got it wrong: A candidate main cause of the counting failure, alongside COUNT-POINTS-01. If they used MATLAB \(inferred in TRAIN-DEFAULTS-01\), its fitgmdist uses no regularization by default and, to my knowledge, stops with an error on a singular covariance, which a one-column cluster like those in Fig. 6c would produce. So they probably set a regularization, or their clusters are wider than they look. Not checked.\nTo close: Ablation on the 45 dB-Hz counting control: reg_covar 1e-3, 1e-2 and 0.1; n_init 1 and 10; plus a MATLAB-default arm \(k-means++ start, 1 replicate, regularization 0, tolerance 1e-6, 100 iterations\). Zero regularization may fail on thin clusters of grid cells, which is itself informative. Then state the chosen settings in the Gate A write-up.)/T(COUNT-EM-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

