2192 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.45 .6 .95]/P 3 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[293.41755 393.0894 422.81568 393.0894 293.41755 378.556 422.81568 378.556]/Rect[289.99189 377.64768 426.24134 393.9977]/AP<</N 2193 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(REAL-EVENT-01: What one false alarm and one detection are on a recording [Paper silent, our choice, impact high]\nWe do: Our protocol \(decision 0004\) scores real recordings with contiguous time splits, guard bands around the attack onset, stated false-alarm operating points and five seeds. For the faithful method one decision would be one satellite's K = 6 map at one epoch: a false alarm on a clean segment \(cleanStatic, or before the onset\), a detection after the onset.\nIf we got it wrong: A different unit or guard band from the comparator paper's makes a benchmark row incomparable even when the detectors are identical.\nTo close: Decide before any run: fix the unit \(one satellite, one K = 6 map, one epoch\) and the guard band in the batch R spec. For each Gate C comparison, adopt that paper's unit where it differs, and label it.)/T(REAL-EVENT-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

2193 0 obj
