2196 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.9 .25 .25]/P 1617 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[125.634609 676.08828 342.95744 676.08828 125.634609 661.5549 342.95744 661.5549]/Rect[122.20894 660.64657 346.3831 676.9966]/AP<</N 2197 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(RES-FIG8-01: Fig. 8 \(Pfa and Pd against the threshold\): never used as a direct target [Not done, impact medium]\nWe do: Phase 1 never scores against Fig. 8. 0053 digitized only trend features \(Pfa floor and highest Pd per C/N0\), and Phase 2's false-alarm fit compared its count-rule floors with them.\nIf we got it wrong: Two of 0053's readings are off. The 36 dB-Hz Pfa floor is 0.625 to 0.713 by my script reading, not 0.50. And "their 36 dB-Hz pair \(Pfa 0.5, Pd 0.29\)" in the status doc and spec does not occur in either figure: Pd 0.29 comes with Pfa about 0.71. The Phase 2 verdict survives, since our GMM count-rule floor at 36 dB-Hz is 0.0025, far from either value. The write-up's "ours rising from 0.005 to 0.79" does not match the json floors, 0.0025 \(36\) to 0.6175 \(45\); the direction holds.\nTo close: Read by script in two passes \(check:fig8a_two_pass\). Remaining: fix targets_fig8.csv, the status doc and 02-reproduction.tex:74. Test: once fused scores are saved \(EVAL-THRESH-01\), plot our Pfa\(gamma\) and Pd\(gamma\) on Fig. 8's axes.)/T(RES-FIG8-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

