2200 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[.98 .82 .2]/P 1617 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[251.2792 647.7894 436.11219 647.7894 251.2792 633.25607 436.11219 633.25607]/Rect[247.85355 632.3477 439.53785 648.69778]/AP<</N 2201 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)/Contents(EVAL-H1H0-01: What the ROC scores as a hit and as a false alarm [Implemented, unverified, impact high]\nWe do: Each test map holds the real signal plus one spoofer 1 dB weaker, 60 to 320 samples and 400 to 800 Hz away. Hits: the tile on the real peak and the tile on the spoofer peak, both positives. False alarms: one noise tile from the same map, half a code period away. No noise-only maps, no clean maps.\nIf we got it wrong: Our peak-against-noise reading follows the results text, and our network scores it at AUC 0.982 at 36 dB-Hz, so it cannot produce their Pd 0.29 at Pfa 0.7 per cell. Phase 2 already tested one map-level alternative, a false alarm as "two or more peaks counted on a clean map": its floor at 36 dB-Hz is 0.0025 against their 0.63, so that reading is out on our maps. What remains untested is the per-map noise reading \(EVAL-CASE-01\). Half our positives are a spoofer 1 dB below the stated C/N0 \(SIG-SPOOFPWR-01\), which lowers our Pd a little.\nTo close: The sources add nothing more that I found \(journal, thesis PDF p68 to p79, Sensors p9 to p16\). Close it with the batch D scan in EVAL-CASE-01, and score it twice: positives as the real peak only, as the spoofer peak only, and as a map-level spoofed-against-clean test \(the framing of the initial work [29]\), to see which one their curves follow.)/T(EVAL-H1H0-01)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

